data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

**All your synchronous Cosmos DB calls will throw at runtime.** In .NET 11 (EF Core 11), the sync-over-async opt-in for the Cosmos provider has been **completely removed**. There is no configuration to restore it.

**Affected methods in your code:**
- `_context.Products.ToList()` → throws
- `_context.Products.First(...)` → throws
- `_context.Products.Count()` → throws
- `_context.SaveChanges()` → throws

**Fix — convert to async:**

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

This means callers must also become `async` — the change propagates up through your call chain. There is no workaround; the Cosmos SDK is async-only and EF Core 11 no longer hides that behind sync wrappers.

**Tracking issue:** https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/issues/37059
